  "title": "Excess-3 Adder (Two Digits in Excess-3 Code)",
  "description": "Design a circuit that adds two decimal digits given in Excess-3 code and produces the sum also in Excess-3 code, along with a decimal carry-out. Use two 7483 ICs and basic gates. Hint: adding two Excess-3 numbers gives an Excess-6 result. If a carry is generated, add 0011 (+3) to correct it; if no carry is generated, add 1101 (-3 in 2's complement) to correct it. The correction word is therefore K' K' K 1 where K is the carry of the first adder.",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "design",
